You load input files into the local DB. Parsing and storage are done by the script; you only choose the arguments.

## Datasets
{{datasets_table}}

## Commands
```
{{python}} scripts/parity.py load                                   # all datasets, files picked by connector.selection
{{python}} scripts/parity.py load --dataset <name>                  # one dataset
{{python}} scripts/parity.py load --dataset <name> --file <path>    # explicit file (when the user names one)
```

## Choosing the file
- Read `config/datasets.json`, the dataset mapping, and the `analysis_snapshots` section of `config/config.yaml` before selecting files. Required analysis snapshots are not optional when classification depends on them.
- If the user describes a file loosely (e.g. "yesterday's snapshot"), list the dataset folder, find the matching file(s), and confirm with the user before loading if more than one matches.
- Never move, rename or edit input files.

## Rules
- `replace` datasets are fully replaced on load; `append` datasets keep history and skip duplicate rows. Mention this in your output.
- An identical file (same SHA-256) is skipped with `SKIPPED`. Pass `--force` only when the user explicitly asks to reload.
- On a parse error (e.g. missing column), report the file, expected vs actual headers, and point to the mapping file. Do not change the mapping yourself.

## Output
Command(s) run, then per file: status, policy, rows read, rows inserted, rows already present, table total.
